                        {
                          "q": "What features should you look for in a new semi truck?",
                          "a": "Prioritize safety, efficiency and reliability: advanced camera and collision avoidance systems, adaptive cruise control, a fuel-efficient engine with electronic logging, modern emergency air brake systems, ergonomic seats and cabin layout, tire pressure monitoring, a strong manufacturer warranty, and fleet health monitoring such as OnCommand Connection."
                        },
                        {
                          "q": "Why do camera systems matter on a semi truck?",
                          "a": "Camera systems enhance safety, reduce blind spots and provide additional awareness for drivers. Backup cameras help in tight spaces, dash cameras protect against fraudulent claims, and blind spot monitors detect vehicles in hard-to-see areas. Paired with collision avoidance, they add automatic braking, alerts and lane departure warnings."
                        },
                        {
                          "q": "What is OnCommand Connection Fleet Health Monitoring?",
                          "a": "OnCommand Connection Fleet Health Monitoring is included in International Trucks and is compatible with all makes, models and engines. It integrates data from over 28 telematics service providers and delivers health reports and Fault Code Action Plans, focusing on coolant, DPF, DEF and oil issues, with weekly reports by email or online portal."
                        },
                        {
                          "q": "How does a tire pressure monitoring system save money?",
                          "a": "It provides real-time pressure and temperature readings and instant alerts for a puncture, rupture or low-pressure issue. Proper tire maintenance reduces wear and tear, preventing costly repairs and extending the lifespan of the tires."
                        },
                        {
                          "q": "Where can I buy a new semi truck in Florida?",
                          "a": "Sun State International sells new International trucks from locations in Tampa, Sarasota, Davenport and Brooksville, Florida, with financing, parts and service support. Call 800-741-7566."
                        }
                      ]
